  "why": "The statement is a single universal claim over all n and all characteristic-0 fields, so one explicit constant-Jacobian map with no polynomial inverse falsifies it as worded: Alpöge's C^3 map is scope whole, direction refuted, object a counterexample; the open plane case is a restriction the statement never singled out, so it does not reduce scope. Alpöge's event is digested via Tao's named public step-by-step digest (and the map is also directly checkable). Gallagher's and Gao's new counterexample families likewise refute the statement but are unreviewed preprints. Tao's digest, the AFP formalisation, Speyer's note, van den Essen's re-derivation of the same map and Prellberg's structural work add no new settlement (none). Hessian, Poisson/Dixmier, characteristic-p, nilpotent-Jacobian, neural and strong-real results are variants. Shaska (graded all-positive weights) and Tian-Sun (Kaliman's weak version, refereed) settle restricted classes: case. The 2024 Preprints.org proof claim is knocked down by the explicit counterexample; older claimed proofs are withdrawn. AI: Alpöge's credit to Fable is close — the direct quote only thanks Fable for 'working overtime', but the AFP entry and tracker report the model found the map; answered generated. Gallagher's own statement of 'substantial mathematical ... assistance' in a human-led construction is assisted.",
  "doubts": "Alpöge's AI role rests on secondary reports of a post the researcher could not read; the basis quote alone is thin, and Wikipedia says the method was not revealed — if the model only searched under human direction, assisted or none would be right. Gallagher's AI quote comes from a fetch summary of the Zenodo page. Constancy of the Jacobian was not independently checked by the researcher, but Tao and the Isabelle entry both state it. Wikipedia and other sources frame the plane case as the remaining open problem; a narrower reading of the statement would make the 2026 events cases.",
